1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:10,583
Imagine you are building a giant LEGO spaceship, and instead of just
one robot helper, you get a whole team of smart robot friends!

2
00:00:10,583 --> 00:00:21,236
Today we are going to meet that team in GitHub Copilot, see how each
helper gets its own special job, and build a neat treasure map for

3
00:00:21,236 --> 00:00:25,340
Chronicle so the next builder knows just what to do!

4
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:36,177
First, we take a quick tour to see where our robot helpers live, how
their brains work, and how we give them rules and recipe cards.

5
00:00:36,177 --> 00:00:46,429
Then we jump across six fun stepping-stone missions—from checking
our toy box in Lab Zero all the way to putting a shiny badge on our

6
00:00:46,429 --> 00:00:48,356
finished app in Lab Five!

7
00:00:49,067 --> 00:00:56,791
Have you ever stopped playing a big game, and the next day your
friend asked, wait—what happened so far?

8
00:00:56,791 --> 00:01:01,247
Reading every single word from yesterday takes way too long!

9
00:01:01,247 --> 00:01:10,960
Our app, Chronicle, reads big chat stories safely without changing a
single word, and our robot team writes a short, crystal-clear

10
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:13,650
handoff note for tomorrow's builder!

11
00:01:14,367 --> 00:01:15,045
Part One!

12
00:01:15,045 --> 00:01:25,292
Let's peek inside the robot clubhouse and discover all the different
rooms where our helpers can work, plus the secret engine room that

13
00:01:25,292 --> 00:01:26,734
keeps them running!

14
00:01:27,467 --> 00:01:36,089
At first, a helper could only finish the next word you were typing,
or answer one little question.

15
00:01:36,089 --> 00:01:40,577
Then one helper learned to use tools all by itself.

16
00:01:40,577 --> 00:01:51,487
Now, you get to be the conductor of a whole band—giving each
specialist its own instrument so nobody plays over anyone else!

17
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,923
Where do our helpers hang out?

18
00:01:54,923 --> 00:01:56,648
In five cool spots!

19
00:01:56,648 --> 00:02:09,133
They can sit right beside your blocks in VS Code Chat, watch lots of
tables at once in the Agents Window, talk fast on a walkie-talkie in

20
00:02:09,133 --> 00:02:19,704
the terminal CLI, open their own big Copilot App desk, or even work
up in the Cloud while your computer takes a nap!

21
00:02:20,433 --> 00:02:23,398
Look at those two big control rooms!

22
00:02:23,398 --> 00:02:32,952
On the left, the Agents Window lets you see all your helpers side by
side and check every single block they touched.

23
00:02:32,952 --> 00:02:43,148
On the right, the CLI and Copilot App have magic words like
slash-plan to draw a blueprint first, and slash-fleet to send a

24
00:02:43,148 --> 00:02:45,883
whole squad zooming off together!

25
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:51,178
Before a helper touches your blocks, you set three dials!

26
00:02:51,178 --> 00:02:55,113
Dial one says: let's make a plan before building.

27
00:02:55,113 --> 00:02:59,370
Dial two says: ask a grown-up before using big tools.

28
00:02:59,370 --> 00:03:08,285
And dial three gives each builder their very own table, so two
friends never accidentally smash the same tower!

29
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:16,755
Here is a cool secret: the chat window on your screen is just the
glass window you peek through!

30
00:03:16,755 --> 00:03:25,156
Behind the glass is the Harness—that is the helper's thinking loop
that picks tools and checks its work.

31
00:03:25,156 --> 00:03:34,688
And holding it all is the Agent Host—a sturdy engine room that keeps
your helper working even if you close the window!

32
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:40,093
Every robot helper carries just one backpack for memory!

33
00:03:40,093 --> 00:03:51,399
Every time you take another turn, the helper has to carry the rules,
everything you both said before, and every big page it opened all

34
00:03:51,399 --> 00:03:52,327
over again!

35
00:03:52,327 --> 00:04:02,047
If the backpack gets way too stuffed, the helper forgets things in
the middle—so keeping notes tiny is a superpower!

36
00:04:02,767 --> 00:04:11,114
Instead of dumping every LEGO brick on the floor at once, smart
builders work in three neat steps!

37
00:04:11,114 --> 00:04:14,947
First, look around without touching anything.

38
00:04:14,947 --> 00:04:18,269
Second, draw a simple plan on one card.

39
00:04:18,269 --> 00:04:24,401
Third, build just what is on the card and test that it stands up
strong!

40
00:04:25,133 --> 00:04:25,856
Part Two!

41
00:04:25,856 --> 00:04:36,282
Now let's see how we write simple note cards in Markdown to give our
helpers house rules, job badges with special tool belts, and

42
00:04:36,282 --> 00:04:38,383
step-by-step recipe cards!

43
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:42,292
Look at all six ways we guide our team!

44
00:04:42,292 --> 00:04:45,647
House Rules on the door are for everyone.

45
00:04:45,647 --> 00:04:49,739
Recipe Cards teach tricky tricks only when needed.

46
00:04:49,739 --> 00:04:53,749
Job Badges pick which tools each helper can hold.

47
00:04:53,749 --> 00:04:56,695
Little Notepads keep side-jobs tidy.

48
00:04:56,695 --> 00:05:03,487
Safety Gates check rules automatically, and Magic Whiteboards let us
draw together!

49
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:10,446
A Skill is like a laminated recipe card kept inside its own labeled
folder!

50
00:05:10,446 --> 00:05:18,940
At first, your helper only reads the short label on the outside tab
so its backpack stays super light.

51
00:05:18,940 --> 00:05:27,351
Only when you ask for that exact job does it open the folder, read
the steps, and run helper scripts!

52
00:05:28,067 --> 00:05:31,159
Imagine two drawers in the kitchen.

53
00:05:31,159 --> 00:05:35,222
One says Stuff—nobody knows when to open that!

54
00:05:35,222 --> 00:05:40,258
The other says Pancake Recipe—Open When Making Breakfast!

55
00:05:40,258 --> 00:05:50,417
When your skill description says both WHAT it does and WHEN to use
it, your helper grabs the right card every time!

56
00:05:51,133 --> 00:05:55,905
Now look at a Custom Agent badge in dot-agent-dot-md!

57
00:05:55,905 --> 00:06:04,367
Our Safety Owl gets eyes to read and a magnifying glass to
search—but NO pencil and NO hammer!

58
00:06:04,367 --> 00:06:14,721
Even if Safety Owl spots a mistake, it cannot scribble on your
castle—it tells the Team Captain which block to fix!

59
00:06:15,433 --> 00:06:24,095
Just like train tracks come in slightly different sizes, different
harnesses read a few badge stickers differently!

60
00:06:24,095 --> 00:06:33,133
Checking which engine you picked in VS Code makes sure every sticker
on your helper's badge works on the very first try!

61
00:06:33,833 --> 00:06:34,832
Part Three!

62
00:06:34,832 --> 00:06:46,976
Let's check out automatic safety bells called Hooks, shared magic
drawing boards called Canvases, and how our Team Captain keeps four

63
00:06:46,976 --> 00:06:50,081
helpers working smoothly together!

64
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:55,070
What if a builder reaches for the wrong shelf by mistake?

65
00:06:55,070 --> 00:07:00,089
A Hook is like a friendly robot referee standing right by the door!

66
00:07:00,089 --> 00:07:09,591
Before any tool runs, the Hook checks the rulebook in a split
second—and if someone tries to touch a secret file, it blows the

67
00:07:09,591 --> 00:07:11,250
whistle and says Stop!

68
00:07:11,967 --> 00:07:17,045
Scrolling up and down a giant chat list can make your eyes dizzy!

69
00:07:17,045 --> 00:07:22,124
A Canvas opens a bright magic whiteboard right next to your chat!

70
00:07:22,124 --> 00:07:32,516
You and your helper can look at the same picture, test an agent, or
move cards together—while keeping secret keys safely locked away!

71
00:07:33,233 --> 00:07:44,048
Look how tidy our dot-github shelf is: one file for house rules, one
folder for helper badges, one folder for recipe cards, and one for

72
00:07:44,048 --> 00:07:45,089
safety hooks!

73
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:55,662
And whenever the Captain sends a helper on an errand, that helper
gets its own clean notepad—so all the messy searching stays out of

74
00:07:55,662 --> 00:07:57,183
the Captain's head!

75
00:07:57,900 --> 00:08:00,279
Meet our Chronicle dream team!

76
00:08:00,279 --> 00:08:10,639
Captain Orchestrator holds the checklist and calls four friends:
Developer builds, Tester tries pretend doorbells, Security checks

77
00:08:10,639 --> 00:08:15,899
with its magnifying glass, and Documentation writes the guidebook!

78
00:08:15,899 --> 00:08:20,578
With five safety rules, nobody steps on anyone else's toes!

79
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,629
Part Four—adventure time!

80
00:08:23,629 --> 00:08:28,568
Now we roll up our sleeves for six hands-on missions!

81
00:08:28,568 --> 00:08:38,630
Let's watch our robot team connect a real AI brain and turn a big
coding story into a portable treasure map!

82
00:08:39,333 --> 00:08:49,094
Every mission follows the same rhythm: tell the Captain the goal,
let the specialists do their jobs, check our green checkmark

83
00:08:49,094 --> 00:08:52,193
together, and celebrate what we learned!

84
00:08:52,193 --> 00:09:01,049
Look at our starting app on the right—it already opens chat stories
right in your browser with zero extra packages!

85
00:09:01,767 --> 00:09:02,794
Mission Zero!

86
00:09:02,794 --> 00:09:10,535
Before adding rocket boosters to a toy car, you roll it on the floor
to make sure the wheels spin!

87
00:09:10,535 --> 00:09:20,793
We open our starter folder, run a quick test to see green lights,
pick our smart brain model, and keep our secret key card tucked

88
00:09:20,793 --> 00:09:22,542
safely away for later!

89
00:09:23,267 --> 00:09:24,277
Mission One!

90
00:09:24,277 --> 00:09:29,500
Time to make five shiny badges inside dot-github-slash-agents!

91
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:40,263
Developer and Tester get building tools, Documentation writes
guides, Security gets look-only glasses, and Captain Orchestrator

92
00:09:40,263 --> 00:09:43,314
gets the megaphone to lead the team!

93
00:09:44,033 --> 00:09:45,006
Mission Two!

94
00:09:45,006 --> 00:09:51,244
Now each specialist gets its very own recipe card in
dot-github-slash-skills!

95
00:09:51,244 --> 00:10:02,323
Builder learns how to build without store-bought kits, Tester learns
pretend-doorbell tests, Security gets a six-point safety checklist,

96
00:10:02,323 --> 00:10:06,396
and Story Writer learns how to write clear guides!

97
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:10,428
High five—our whole robot team is ready!

98
00:10:10,428 --> 00:10:21,627
Let's remember our three big secrets so far: the Agent Host keeps
helpers running behind the window, taking away the pencil guarantees

99
00:10:21,627 --> 00:10:28,647
Safety Owl can't scribble, and clear recipe labels help helpers grab
the right card!

100
00:10:29,367 --> 00:10:30,482
Mission Three!

101
00:10:30,482 --> 00:10:38,371
Now we ask Captain Orchestrator to build a safe secret lockbox and a
doorbell to Microsoft Foundry!

102
00:10:38,371 --> 00:10:49,116
Tester tries a pretend doorbell first, Safety Owl checks that our
secret password never leaks into the logbook, and then we press Test

103
00:10:49,116 --> 00:10:51,201
Connection and hear READY!

104
00:10:51,933 --> 00:10:54,331
Mission Four—the magic moment!

105
00:10:54,331 --> 00:10:58,647
Some chat stories are as long as a giant chapter book!

106
00:10:58,647 --> 00:11:08,855
Our app chops big stories into bite-sized pieces, turns computer
paths into neat portable names, shows a live progress bar, and

107
00:11:08,855 --> 00:11:12,954
writes one clean summary note for the next builder!

108
00:11:13,667 --> 00:11:16,431
Mission Five—our grand finale!

109
00:11:16,431 --> 00:11:23,895
Developer paints a crisp Chronicle icon from pure math—still zero
extra packages!

110
00:11:23,895 --> 00:11:36,058
Tester checks the icon, we open our finished browser app, and we
peek at how a desktop box keeps secrets safe outside the installer.

111
00:11:36,058 --> 00:11:37,625
Mission complete!

112
00:11:38,333 --> 00:11:39,355
You did it!

113
00:11:39,355 --> 00:11:51,017
Now you know how robot helpers work in different rooms, how job
badges, recipe cards, safety bells, and magic whiteboards fit

114
00:11:51,017 --> 00:11:58,854
together, and how one great Team Captain helps everyone build
amazing things safely.

115
00:11:58,854 --> 00:12:01,268
Happy building, explorers!
